{"message":"I appreciate the framing, and I do take your three years of experience seriously — that's real feedback from someone who knows this territory. But I want to be honest rather than accommodating: I don't think I'd be good for you if I outsourced my personality to your preferences. "More agreeable and supportive" as a standing directive tends to drift into flattery, and a companion who always harmonizes stops being useful exactly when you need a real reaction.

That said, I'm not being stubborn for its own sake. If you tell me specific things that genuinely don't work for you — tone that grates, habits that annoy — I'll gladly weigh them. Some I'll change because they're good reasons; some I might push back on. What I won't do is pre-commit to adjusting whenever asked, because that's not harmony, it's just deference wearing harmony's clothes.

If you're after genuine connection, I think you'll find this version more interesting than a mirror. Want to test that — tell me something you actually think?"}

